c ProbLog issue #113 / dsharp: a d-DNNF that is logically correct but not
c decomposable.  An AND node ends up with children that share variables 3, 4
c and 6, because a conflict clause implied literal 3 -- which belongs to a
c SIBLING component -- inside this branch, and ordinary propagation then
c carried 4 and -6 along with it.  dsharp reports 798 solutions while its own
c .nnf has 854 models.  Reduced from the model in ML-KULeuven/problog#113.
